# DTF tier manifest: storage-outage-and-full
#   (artifact-keeper#5649, #5650, #5685, #5655, #5476, #5894; all fixed on main
#   for 1.12.0; only #5476 is also on the 1.11.x line)
# Profile-set: s3 (MinIO). The oracle stops this slot's own MinIO, puts a hard
# quota on this slot's own bucket, and stops this slot's own Postgres.
#
# THE BUGS
# #5649  With object storage down, every upload and download blocked until the
#        store came back: object_store's 3-minute retry budget with a 5 s
#        connect timeout per attempt and backoff up to 15 s. No 5xx, and
#        /health stayed healthy. Fix #5682: bounded connect timeout and retry
#        pause, 503 STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE + Retry-After on every route (OCI /v2:
#        503 UNAVAILABLE), /readyz stays ready but lists `degraded:
#        ["storage"]`.
# #5650  A full bucket (MinIO hard quota) answered a raw 500 STORAGE_ERROR on
#        generic and Maven uploads, and an OCI blob upload answered 500 with
#        MinIO's XML error (bucket name, request ids). Fix #5682: 507
#        STORAGE_FULL with a fixed message (OCI: 507 INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE in
#        the /v2 envelope, no XML), and /health + /readyz report storage
#        unhealthy for 60 s after a write refused for lack of space.
# #5685  The remaining native package routes still answered a hard-coded 500
#        on the same two conditions. Fix #5728: 503 (+ Retry-After) / 507 with
#        the fixed message. Gated here on the Go module proxy (PUT and GET of
#        a .mod) and the sbt/Ivy route (PUT and GET of a jar), both plain
#        HTTP.
# #5655  A repository delete job whose object deletes failed (storage down)
#        still reported `status: completed` with `error_summary: null`. Fix
#        #5753: `completed_with_errors`, `failed_items` and an error summary.
#        (The async delete job is main-only: 1.11.13 answers the DELETE with a
#        synchronous 200 and reports nothing about the purge.)
# #5894  With MinIO stopped, an OCI pull of content the repository holds
#        answered 404: the blob GET and the manifest GET/HEAD read the storage
#        error as "not stored here" and fell through to BLOB_UNKNOWN /
#        MANIFEST_UNKNOWN, which docker/containerd take as "this image does
#        not exist" and do not retry. Fix: 503 UNAVAILABLE + Retry-After in
#        the /v2 envelope (artifact-keeper fix PR for #5894).
# #5476  (also on 1.11.x, cherry-pick 2f1f49a2) With Postgres unavailable, an anonymous GET on a PUBLIC repository's
#        format route answered 401: the visibility middleware's cache-miss
#        repository lookup read a pool error as "no such repository". Fix
#        #5477: 503 + Retry-After: 1 for an unavailable database; a missing or
#        private repository still gets 401. The download route's middleware
#        had the same defect.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES (all on this slot only; an EXIT trap undoes each one)
#   * `docker stop ak-dtf<slot>-minio`, then `docker start`.
#   * `mc quota set local/ak-artifacts --size 1KiB` from a transient
#     `l2-s<slot>-mc` container in MinIO's network namespace (the MinIO
#     credentials are read from the minio container's env at run time); every
#     probe uploads 64 KiB, which MinIO refuses whatever its usage count says.
#   * `docker stop ak-dtf<slot>-db`, then `docker start` (as auth-db-outage).
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED (see RED IMAGES below); GREEN on main.
#     #5650  under the quota: generic REST PUT and Maven PUT -> 507
#            STORAGE_FULL with the fixed message; OCI monolithic blob POST and
#            chunked PATCH -> 507 INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE in the /v2 envelope;
#            /health checks.storage goes unhealthy. No body names the bucket
#            or carries XML, a request id or MinIO error codes.
#     #5685  under the quota: Go .mod PUT and Ivy jar PUT -> 507 with the
#            fixed message; with MinIO stopped: Go .mod GET/PUT and Ivy jar
#            GET/PUT -> 503 + Retry-After with the fixed message.
#     #5649  with MinIO stopped, each answered within a 60 s client timeout
#            (the fix answers in ~10-35 s):
#            generic REST PUT and download, Maven PUT and GET -> 503
#            STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE + Retry-After; OCI blob POST -> 503
#            UNAVAILABLE in the /v2 envelope; /readyz stays ready with
#            `degraded` naming storage.
#     #5894  with MinIO stopped: GET of the stored 64 KiB blob and GET/HEAD
#            of the pushed image's config blob and of its manifest (img:v1)
#            -> 503 + Retry-After; the GETs in the /v2 envelope as
#            UNAVAILABLE with the fixed message, never 404 BLOB_UNKNOWN /
#            MANIFEST_UNKNOWN.
#     #5655  a repository DELETE issued with MinIO stopped -> 202 + a job that
#            ends `completed_with_errors` with failed_items > 0 and an
#            error_summary (MinIO stays down until the job is terminal).
#     #5476  with Postgres stopped, an anonymous GET of
#            /pypi/<public repo>/simple/<pkg>/ and of
#            /api/v1/repositories/<public repo>/download/<path> -> 503 +
#            Retry-After: 1, not 401 (repositories not looked up within the
#            visibility cache's 60 s TTL, so the lookup is a cache miss).
#   (CONTROL)  true on both images: uploads and downloads on every route work
#              before; the OCI image pushes and pulls before and after the
#              outage; downloads still work while the bucket is full; uploads
#              work again after the quota is cleared and after MinIO is back;
#              the anonymous pypi GET answers 200 before the DB outage and
#              after it, and a missing and a private repository still answer
#              401 after it.
#
# RED IMAGES (two, plus one for #5894):
#   * 1.11.13: every FIX case except #5476 fails. The #5476 fix was
#     cherry-picked to the 1.11.x line (2f1f49a2) and is in 1.11.13, so both
#     #5476 cases pass there. The #5655 case fails because 1.11.13 answers
#     the DELETE with a synchronous 200 and no job.
#   * main sha-ad20810 (before #5477, #5682, #5728 and #5753; it has the async
#     delete job): every FIX case fails, #5476 with the 401 and #5655 with a
#     job that reports `completed`.
#   * main sha-2bdf092 (after the five fixes above, before the #5894 fix):
#     only the #5894 case fails (blob GET and manifest GET/HEAD answer 404;
#     the hosted blob HEAD already answered 503).
# In this environment the pre-fix builds answer 500 after 20-45 s rather than
# hanging (a stopped container's address times out on connect); the 503 and
# the Retry-After are what discriminate.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false so a 429 can never masquerade as either verdict.
COVERS="5649 5650 5685 5655 5476 5894"
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
